 used  the swabs are collected they go into a  collection media  and some of that is loaded onto the  instrument and you run it  and within about 30 minutes  and three simple steps you get a result  the read  reader is a lateral flow  unit and so you have some  readout in terms of certain lines on the  lateral flow instrument that correspond  to the control  and a positive line for  indicating presence of the virus  this has been  will  considerably improve the turnaround time  and speed things up so if i go to the  next slide then we want to talk about  the other kit that we recently got an  eoa approval for in a couple of months  ago  this is the version 2 of our combo kit  and one of the things we did here is to  increase the confidence in the results  in this particular case we have about  eight  targets within the essay  three of them uh  i mean  in three regions the rf1a the rf1b and  the n-genes and this compensates for any  new emerging sas virus mutations so  having degeneracy the number of targets  makes the essay extremely robust it's  very sensitive the  limit of detection is around 75 gc's per  amount it's more sensitive than the  version one that we had and it's  affordable and scalable  and easily added onto your testing menu  on the same instruments that i mentioned  before  the other part where we work is in  surveillance these are reo products  and they can be used to detect variants  so one workflow that we generally talk  about is detection and identification of  source coverage variants so if you have  a positive sample  in an initial screening test if the  sample comes up positive  then it can go in for variance screening  which can be done  by using genotyping assays  or  by amplicon based sequencing on a single  instrument  you can also use the ion tolerance to  get complete viral characterization so  this sequence all of the positive  samples can be sequenced and in general  gives you a good result in terms of  getting your entire  the plate